<div class="landing">
  <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <span class="eyebrow">THE MATERIAL COMPONENT LIBRARY</span>
    <h1 class="hero__name" id="hero-title">Material Design.<br><span class="hero__accent">Made for the web.</span></h1>
    <p class="hero__tagline">Expressive components. Your framework.<br>A little TypeScript, a lot of possibility.</p>
    <div class="hero__actions"><a class="btn btn--primary" href="/components/button/">Explore components <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/docs/">Read the docs</a></div>
    <div class="hero__install"><%~ it.install %></div>
    <div class="hero__notes"><span>Material Design 3</span><span>Zero runtime dependencies</span><span>Open source</span></div>
  </section>
  <div class="landing-features">
    <div><span class="feature-index">01 / EXPLORE</span><h2>Find the right expression.</h2><p>Try variants, sizes, and shapes in a live component playground.</p></div>
    <div><span class="feature-index">02 / CUSTOMIZE</span><h2>Make it feel like you.</h2><p>Switch Material themes and light or dark mode. See every change as you make it.</p></div>
    <div><span class="feature-index">03 / BUILD</span><h2>Take it from here.</h2><p>Copy your configuration and bring the component to your project. No framework required.</p></div>
  </div>
  <footer class="landing-footer"><span>material · Built by <a href="https://floor.io">floor</a></span><a href="https://github.com/floor/material">Source on GitHub ↗</a></footer>
</div>
